      summary: "Wilmington Trust, representing bondholders in a commercial mortgage pool, sued Nakash Lincoln LLC and Lincoln 1816 LLC in Cook County on Aug. 14, 2026, alleging they failed to repay a $25.4 million loan on the land at 1816 North Clark Street when it matured earlier this year. The suit seeks the owner's fee interest and landlord rights in the land under Hotel Lincoln, and leaves the hotel's ground lease and leasehold, held by a separate Nakash-led entity, in place, The Real Deal reported. The hotel building has its own $35 million loan, which is not part of this case.",
