      summary: "A St. Louis County judge in September 2025 upheld Brentwood, Missouri's blight designation of properties along the Manchester Road Corridor, which would let the city use eminent domain for a $436 million redevelopment plan, Reason reported. Judge Kristine Allen Kerr held that the designation was 'fairly debatable' and that the city had not acted arbitrarily and capriciously. The plaintiffs appealed; the Missouri Supreme Court denied their application to transfer the case from the Court of Appeals in April 2026.",
