      summary: "Waukesha State Bank sued 225 East Michigan Street LLC, an affiliate of J. Jeffers & Co., in Milwaukee County Circuit Court on August 3, 2026, alleging it defaulted on a $6.57 million loan on the historic Mackie Building and owed $6.2 million, including $5.9 million in principal. Developer Joshua Jeffers attributed the default to lower percentage rent from anchor tenant The Grain Exchange. The Milwaukee Journal Sentinel reported that Judge William Pocan dismissed the suit by stipulation on September 14 and that a companion money-judgment suit in Waukesha County was dismissed the next day; Jeffers said the loan had been reinstated.",
