      summary: "Developer Brian O'Neill filed land-use appeals on September 16, 2026 in Montgomery County Court of Common Pleas against the Upper Merion Township Board of Supervisors, seeking to reverse its unanimous August 13 denial of five data center plans totaling about 4.6 million square feet, The Philadelphia Inquirer reported. The suits claim the board acted in bad faith after officials had said data centers qualify as permitted warehouses. Township officials declined to comment pending review. In October, PhillyVoice reported, the developers withdrew related zoning hearing board applications while pursuing the court challenges.",
