      summary: "A commercial developer's lawsuit against the City of Fresno over 100 free parking spaces near his Grand 1401 building was set for a jury trial beginning October 12, 2026 before Fresno County Superior Court Judge D. Tyler Tharpe, GV Wire reported. He says the city, under then-Mayor Ashley Swearengin, promised the spaces to help bring anchor tenant Tutor Perini downtown; the city disputes that such an agreement existed. Construction of a new city parking garage has cut off access to the spaces, and he says losing Tutor Perini could cost him more than $7 million.",
