      summary: "The Oklahoma Department of Securities sued Vesta Realty, LLC on August 24, 2026, alleging the Tulsa-based multifamily company failed to provide subpoenaed documents, including the identities of and communications with investors in some of the limited liability companies under the Vesta umbrella, Oklahoma Watch reported. The department has asked the district court to order the records produced. CEO Marc Kulick told Oklahoma Watch the company is 'in the process of engaging an attorney' and looks forward to resolving the matter.",
