      summary: "On October 6, 2026, New York's Appellate Division, First Department unanimously affirmed the dismissal of a commercial tenant's suit against its landlord, ESRT Empire State Building LLC. The court held that the tenant had expressly waived its constructive eviction rights in the lease, and that even without the waiver it had not shown the substantial loss of use the claim requires. Its breach-of-lease claim also failed because it identified no lease provision that was breached.",
