      summary: "The parents of a 17-year-old killed in an April 23, 2026 shooting in the food court of the Mall of Louisiana in Baton Rouge filed a wrongful-death and negligence suit on Oct. 7, 2026 in the 19th Judicial District Court, Acadiana News First reported. The defendants are Mall of Louisiana LLC, Brookfield Properties Retail Inc. and Marksman Security LLC, described as the mall's owner, its operator/manager and its security contractor, along with the person accused of the shooting. Four people who were with the teen, two of whom were shot, joined as plaintiffs.",
