      seoTitle: "NY Court Revives $1M Sublease Fight Over Sublessor's Utilities",
      seoDescription: "A New York appeals court reversed a $1M rent judgment against sublessees, finding their claim the sublessor failed on utilities and gas raised a triable issue.",
      title: "VK Dental Group, Inc. v. Tender Touch Physical Therapy, PLLC (NY Appellate Division Revives $1M Sublease Rent Dispute)",
      brief: "New York's Second Department reversed a $1,004,426.20 sublease rent judgment for VK Dental Group, finding the sublessees' claim that VK breached on utilities and gas service raised a triable issue.",
      category: "lease-disputes",
      status: "ruling",
      date: "2026-10-21",
      jurisdiction: "Appellate Division, Second Department, New York",
      state: "NY",
      propertyType: null,
      amount: "$1,004,426.20 judgment reversed",
      amountUsd: 1004426.2,
      amountBasis: "judgment",
      source: "live",
      sourceUrl: "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/11042103/vk-dental-group-inc-v-tender-touch-physical-therapy-pllc/",
      summary: "New York's Appellate Division, Second Department on October 21, 2026 reversed a $1,004,426.20 judgment that sublessor VK Dental Group, Inc. had won against Tender Touch Physical Therapy, PLLC and the other sublessees for unpaid rent. The court held that VK Dental showed the rent went unpaid, but the sublessees raised a triable issue of fact with their principal's affidavit stating that VK Dental failed to pay 50% of utilities as the subleases required and had the gas service disconnected. It denied VK Dental's motion for summary judgment.",
      significance: "A breach-of-contract plaintiff in New York must prove its own performance, and here a sworn statement that the sublessor failed its own sublease obligations was enough to defeat summary judgment on a seven-figure rent claim. The court did not decide whether the sublessor actually breached; it held only that the factual dispute precluded summary judgment.",
      body: [
        "New York's Appellate Division, Second Department ruled on October 21, 2026 that sublessor VK Dental Group, Inc. was not entitled to summary judgment on its claims for unpaid sublease rent, reversing a Supreme Court, Kings County judgment of $1,004,426.20 against Tender Touch Physical Therapy, PLLC and the other sublessees. The decision and order was issued by a four-justice panel.",
        "According to the decision, in January 2017 Metrotech Smile Dental, P.C. leased property from 350 Fulton Realty, LLC, which is not a party. In March 2017 Metrotech subleased the premises to the defendants, and in April 2018 it assigned its lease to VK Dental, which became the sublessor.",
        "VK Dental sued in May 2022, alleging the sublessees failed to pay rent and that it was forced to surrender possession of the premises. After a hearing at which a VK Dental witness testified, the trial court granted summary judgment in an order dated October 21, 2024, and entered judgment on November 21, 2024.",
        "The Second Department held that, even setting aside the hearing testimony, VK Dental showed the sublessees had not paid rent for certain months. But the sublessees' principal stated in an affidavit that VK Dental failed to pay 50% of utilities as the subleases required and had the gas service disconnected. Because a breach-of-contract plaintiff must prove its own performance, that raised a triable issue of fact. The court reversed the judgment, denied the summary judgment motion, dismissed the separate appeal from the order because it merged into the judgment, and awarded the sublessees one bill of costs."
      ],
      tags: ["commercial-lease", "sublease", "summary-judgment", "new-york", "medical-office"],
